From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 05:02:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 212/215] feat: factor the volumetric cloud shape and density
 functions into CloudsCommon.cfi

Preparation for decision 09 section 9.2 (volumetric clouds in ray traced
reflections): the secondary cloud march in ShadePS must evaluate the SAME
density field the direct view does, so the shape/density block of Clouds.cfx
becomes a shared .cfi instead of being duplicated.

Moved verbatim out of Clouds.cfx (its lines 56-372) into the new
Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/CloudsCommon.cfi, included by Clouds.cfx at
exactly the place the code used to sit:

  acos_fast
  vcGetLinearDepth
  GetVdC
  vcTranslateWorldPosToCloudPos
  vcGetIntersectionPlane
  vcGetIntersectionWithCloudLayer
  GetFBM
  vcGetCloudBlockerInfluence
  vcGetAllCloudBlockersInfluence
  struct CloudGenParam
  GetCloudDensity
  GetOpticalThickness

CloudBaseDensityTexture (t15) deliberately stays declared in Clouds.cfx, above
the include: it is a resource declaration and does not belong in a file a
second shader includes.

The only text added to the moved block is two opt-outs for an includer whose
%_RT_SAMPLE3 / %_RT_SAMPLE4 bits mean something else - in Total_Illumination.cfx
the same two bits are "pre-baked diffuse cache" and "diffuse pass", and letting
SAMPLE3 through there would sample CloudBaseDensityTexture at a register the
ShadePass technique has bound to something else. Clouds.cfx defines neither
symbol, so its preprocessed text is unchanged.

No behaviour change. Verified by expanding the include back into Clouds.cfx,
resolving the two opt-outs as Clouds.cfx resolves them, and diffing against
3f33313a: IDENTICAL (scene-notes/rt/tools/clouds_move_check.py). cryfx_lint.py
reports 0 findings on both files.

This is the merge point for the paused clouds branch: its edits to those twelve
functions move into CloudsCommon.cfi unchanged.

